 the iran  nuclear deal he said he hopes that the  u.s  would not go back to the old  nuclear deal that is currently discussed  with the international  community and what we just heard also in  the uh  from prime minister netanyahu talked  about peace but mainly peace with the  arab nations the abrahamic courts he was  referring to  but also he talked about the  humanitarian situation in gaza  and he conditioned that that it needs to  get better there but he conditioned that  also on the return of  the missing soldiers and also the two  israelis that are held in  that are being held in gaza now anthony  blinken the u.s secretary of state  addressed more the humanitarian  situation he said it's a very  difficult situation in gaza and that he  would  make a major announcement on  rehabilitation and rebuilding gaza  but also the need to make sure that this  doesn't benefit hamas  and he only brushed the issue of the  iran nuclear deal  very very briefly we know that he wants  to stabilize  the ceasefire that's in place but tanya  looking ahead is it realistic to expect  any steps towards israeli-palestinian  peace talks  well that's actually the question here  because at the moment the focus seems to  be to securing  the ceasefire that was broken by egypt  between hamas and  israel and to focus on rehabilitation or  reconstruction of gaza that is a very  that is needed there needs to be also  you know discussion about  a mechanism to bring in uh for example  building materials so we are there at  the very very beginning of this  although the u.s secretary of state  anthony blinken addressed  he said you know there needs to be an  address of the  underlying causes for this conflict but  you know we didn't get a sense that  anything is being done  in this regard to to find also a  political  uh uh solution to all of this we have  here at the very beginning it seems  and at the same time we understand also  it's important for the american  administration at least  you know to re-strengthen ties with the  palestinian authority  in the occupied west bank he's going to  meet the palestinian president mahmoud  abbas now in the afternoon  because these ties had been strained  under the trump administration  our correspondent tanya kramer reporting  from jerusalem thank you
 

